{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgNbagU0mHVrO3s6Hzk5g","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The bug is that I set fills on the instance frame, so each Icon_Cart instance renders as one solid square; the fix is to clear the instance's own fills and recolor its descendant vectors instead. I write a repair function that walks the library, and for each INSTANCE whose mainComponent name starts with 'Icon_', clears fills and sets descendant vector fills. The same applies to the header Actions. I also widen oldWrap from 120 to 140 and shrink the old price text to 14, since the price row is 253 wide inside the 285 card with 16 padding and \"Rs. 2,500,000.00\" overflows. For future scripts I use a proper icon() helper. The feature strip screenshot is 458 wide with 4 black squares and no text, so I fix icons first and re-screenshot.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation_input_tokens":3990,"input_tokens":55,"cache_read_input_tokens":68096,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3990}},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aeaa83eb-a2d5-49ac-8120-9a0636e2bfb4","uuid":"555ac3a3-32aa-4b24-9b1f-90ef391d540d","timestamp":"2026-11-01T19:18:09.670Z","thinking_duration_ms":14102}
